// A C handle's method without a body is a C binding, named by `@c`; a static one needs a body, and a
// method with a body is not bound.
// error: `unbound` has no body, so it is a C binding, and names its C function with `@c("<prototype>")`
// error: `size` is static, so it needs a body: a C handle's methods without one are C bindings
// error: `size` is static, so it needs a body: it belongs to `WithMethods` itself
// error: a C binding has no body: the C function its prototype names is its body

@c(type: "struct thing *", release: "free")
class WithMethods
    unbound() -> int
    @c("int thing_size(struct thing *self)")
    static size() -> int
    @c("int thing_size(struct thing *self)")
    bodied() -> int = 3

main() = 0
